<article class="env-lemma" id="04JQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04JQ">Lemma <span data-tag="04JQ">59.59.1</span>.</a> Let $S = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)$ with $K$ a field. Let $\overline{s}$ be a geometric point of $S$. Let $G = \text{Gal}_{\kappa (s)}$ denote the absolute Galois group. The stalk functor induces an equivalence of categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \textit{Ab}(S_{\acute{e}tale}) \longrightarrow \text{Mod}_ G, \quad \mathcal{F} \longmapsto \mathcal{F}_{\overline{s}}.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In Theorem <a href="/tag/03QT" data-tag="03QT">59.56.3</a> we have seen the equivalence between sheaves of sets and $G$-sets. The current lemma follows formally from this as an abelian sheaf is just a sheaf of sets endowed with a commutative group law, and a $G$-module is just a $G$-set endowed with a commutative group law. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>